### Minecraft Modding ###
run/
!**/src/**/run/
# NeoGradle writes one directory per run configuration - runs/client, runs/server - and everything
# in them is generated: game assets, logs, options.txt, and the diagnostics markers next to them.
runs/
**/src/generated/**/.cache/
repo/
!**/src/**/repo/

### Run output ###
# A `runClient` writes its stdout beside the module, and a frame or window dump writes a PNG there
# too. Both are read while a bug is being chased rather than kept, which is the same reason `runs/`
# above is ignored: what a run produces belongs to that run.
/run-stdout.log
/runclient*.log
/build-*.log
/gl-calls.txt
/*.png
